.git
.gitignore
tests/
docs/
images/
*.md
!README.md
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.osm_cache/
data/

# Synology DSM housekeeping folders that live at the root of every
# shared folder, invisible in File Station but very real on disk -
# confirmed on Christer's NAS: #recycle alone held 83G (the shared
# folder's Recycle Bin - files "deleted" through DSM land here
# instead of actually being removed), which is why "docker-compose
# build bv-web" printed "Sending build context to Docker daemon
# 88.56GB" and then sat silent for minutes before Step 1 even showed
# - Docker doesn't print anything while gathering/tar-ing the
# context. A leading '#' starts a comment in .dockerignore (same
# convention as .gitignore), so it has to be escaped as '\#recycle'
# to actually match a folder literally named "#recycle" - a bare
# "#recycle" line here would have been silently ignored.
\#recycle/
@eaDir/
